</section>

<section>
  <h2>Fast Particle Updates on Robot Meshes</h2>
  <p>
    The robot mesh is preprocessed into nearly uniform faces, and geodesic distances between faces on each link are computed offline. A particle can
    then move over the surface through a lookup and face-index update. For a proposed contact location, a convex quadratic program finds forces
    consistent with the sensor measurements and a polyhedral friction cone. Its residual determines the particle weight.
  </p>
